.TH BLUETOOTH-SEND 1 "October 2026" "scripts" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bluetooth-send \- send files to a paired mobile phone via Bluetooth using blueman-sendto
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bluetooth-send
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-\-setup\fR [\fIMAC\fR]]
[\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBbluetooth-send\fR transmits selected files to a paired mobile phone over Bluetooth using \fBblueman-sendto\fR.
.PP
The destination device MAC address is resolved dynamically and securely without hardcoding personal hardware identifiers
into repositories:
.IP 1. 4
\fBBLUETOOTH_PHONE_MAC\fR environment variable.
.IP 2. 4
\fB$HOME/.config/scripts/bluetooth_phone.mac\fR.
.IP 3. 4
\fB$HOME/.config/scripts/bluetooth_phone.conf\fR.
.IP 4. 4
Automatic discovery of a single paired phone device via \fBbluetoothctl\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-setup " [" \fIMAC\fR "]"
Interactively configure or persist the specified Bluetooth MAC address into \fB$HOME/.config/scripts/bluetooth_phone.mac\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Displays brief command-line help and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR blueman-sendto (1),
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.BR scripts (1)
